# Python

- Imports: stdlib, then third-party, then `pia.*`. All at module top. No unused imports.
- Only allowed lazy import: Playwright inside the ingest review path so Streamlit Cloud never imports it.
- Comments only for non-obvious constraints. Public modules get a one-line docstring.
- Package with `uv` only (`uv add` / `uv lock` / `uv run`). Never `pip install`.
- Repositories do not call tools or LLMs. Services do not embed SQL/PostgREST.
- Logging via `pia.logging.get_logger`. Never log secrets, HTML, unbounded review text, or raw user queries.
- Default pytest uses fakes and committed fixtures. No network. DeepEval only under `eval` or `conversation` markers.
